imbridge link previews: fetch-link {url, directory, timeout?} loads a page's preview with LinkPresentation, as Messages
does when you paste a link, and archives it with LPMessagesPayload (the "RichLink" payload of Messages' URL balloon),
saving the pictures it refers to as .pluginPayloadAttachment files in directory; it replies with the payload (base64)
and the files, or found: NO. send-link {chatGuid, url, payload, attachments, guid?} sends the URL as text in a URL
balloon with that payload, its pictures as transfers hidden from the transcript, in the payload's order. Two steps, so
the caller can check where a preview came from before anything is sent.

